IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `cdba-nouns`
IMPORT `cdba-reg-appeals`

-- Tests for Regulations ss 20 to 29, with the working beside each assertion.

§ `Regulations s 20 -- tests`

-- s 20(2): a decision of no benefit, of the amount, or of a penalty goes first to the
-- Minister under s 18.
#ASSERT `how the person may challenge the decision` `a decision that no benefit be paid to the person` EQUALS `ask the Minister to reconsider it under section 18`
#ASSERT `how the person may challenge the decision` `a decision respecting the amount of a benefit that the person has received or will receive` EQUALS `ask the Minister to reconsider it under section 18`
#ASSERT `how the person may challenge the decision` `a decision imposing a penalty under section 35` EQUALS `ask the Minister to reconsider it under section 18`
-- s 20(2) and (3): only the Minister's decisions under s 18(4) and s 19(4) go to the Tribunal.
#ASSERT `how the person may challenge the decision` `a decision on a request for reconsideration made under subsection 18(4)` EQUALS `appeal it to the Social Security Tribunal`
#ASSERT `how the person may challenge the decision` `a decision on a request for an extension of time made under subsection 19(4)` EQUALS `appeal it to the Social Security Tribunal`
-- Any other decision: the text states no route.
#ASSERT `how the person may challenge the decision` `any other decision` EQUALS `the text states no route`

§ `Regulations ss 21 and 29 -- tests`

#ASSERT `who decides the ground of appeal` TRUE EQUALS `the Tax Court of Canada, on a reference from the Social Security Tribunal`
#ASSERT `who decides the ground of appeal` FALSE EQUALS `the Social Security Tribunal`
#ASSERT `the Social Security Tribunal must now proceed on the grounds not referred, under its Rules of Procedure` TRUE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT `the Social Security Tribunal must now proceed on the grounds not referred, under its Rules of Procedure` TRUE FALSE
#ASSERT NOT `the Social Security Tribunal must now proceed on the grounds not referred, under its Rules of Procedure` FALSE TRUE

§ `Regulations s 23 -- tests`

#ASSERT `the other person is added as a party to the appeal` TRUE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT `the other person is added as a party to the appeal` TRUE FALSE
#ASSERT NOT `the other person is added as a party to the appeal` FALSE TRUE

§ `Regulations s 24 -- tests`

#ASSERT `where the hearing of a reference is held` FALSE EQUALS `the city, town or village in which, or nearest to which, the appellant is ordinarily resident`
#ASSERT `where the hearing of a reference is held` TRUE EQUALS `another place, or by audioconference or videoconference, with the appellant's written consent`
#ASSERT `the Registrar must notify the appellant by registered mail of the date, place and time` TRUE
#ASSERT NOT `the Registrar must notify the appellant by registered mail of the date, place and time` FALSE

§ `Regulations ss 26 and 28 -- tests`

#ASSERT `the judge may require written submissions` TRUE
#ASSERT NOT `the judge may require written submissions` FALSE
#ASSERT NOT `costs may be awarded or fees charged to the appellant on a reference`
